-- title:
--   From HTo G Type Filtered Outcome Sum
-- statement:
--   **Partitioning completed-outcome tuples by type does not change their sum.**
--
--   Let $n\in\mathbb{N}$, let $\mathcal O_n$ be the finite set of completed-outcome tuples, let $\tau(gs)\in\{0,1\}^n$ record genuine positions, and let $R$ be an additive commutative monoid. For every $F$ with values in $R$,
--
--   $$
--   \sum_{\tau\in\{0,1\}^n}\sum_{\substack{gs\in\mathcal O_n:\tau(gs)=\tau}}F(\tau,gs)=\sum_{gs\in\mathcal O_n}F(\tau(gs),gs).
--   $$
--
--   Every tuple lies in exactly one type fiber. This finite reindexing identity is used by the Boolean and type-filtered versions and by the averaged-sandwich total calculation.
--
--   Formalization credit: Sirui Lu, Ruixuan Deng, Yanqiao Zhu, and Zhengfeng Ji (arXiv:2609.19814). Mathematical source: Zhengfeng Ji, Anand Natarajan, Thomas Vidick, John Wright, and Henry Yuen (arXiv:2009.12982).
--
